3"/></fig><fig id="fig4" position="float"><label>Figure 4</label><caption><p>(<italic>a</italic>,<italic>b</italic>) Final epidemic size against number of infectious nodes after one infectious period: logarithmic <italic>x</italic>-axis and only two network representations shown, for clarity (<italic>b</italic>).</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="rspb20081009f04"/></fig><fig id="fig5" position="float"><label>Figure 5</label><caption><p>(<italic>a</italic>,<italic>b</italic>) Frequency distribution (from 100&#x0200a;000&#x0200a;000 runs) of final epidemic sizes from 28-day weighted static and dynamic network representations; simulations halted after 28 model time steps in each case. Transmission probability, <italic>&#x003bd;</italic>=0.9; infectious period, <italic>&#x003bc;</italic>=8 (<italic>a</italic>); transmission probability for 28-day weighted static representation adjusted to <italic>&#x003bd;</italic>=0.8327 to give same mean final epidemic size as the dynamic network representation (<italic>b</italic>).</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="rspb20081009f05"/></fig></floats-wrap></article>